WEBVTT

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:07.690
It was August 31st, 2035.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.540
Aloha!

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.950
Here's some macadamia chocolates I brought from Hawaii as a gift!

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:05.960
...and they're not listening...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.830
Well then, how about cellphone straps from Sokoichi?

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.830
Note: Sokoichi is a parody of Kokoichi (Kokoichibanya), a huge curry restaurant chain that has a campaign offering cellphone straps, as well.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:11.340
You won't believe it; they have Sokoichi in Hawaii-

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:11.340
Note: Kokoichi also has chains in Hawaii.

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:13.380
Ah, I'm sorry.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.810
Quiet!!!

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:21.000
Look, turn around now

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:25.330
but things like chances won't be there anymore.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:29.790
That's what some people will tell you,

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:36.040
but there are just times when you can't move at all.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.520
Yes, everything I say

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:49.960
is for your sake.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.480
Sorry, but

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.770
I won't consent easily

00:01:55.030 --> 00:02:00.670
to things I don't accept.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:07.650
Even if I can get by that moment with a lie

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.730
I'll end up regretting it afterwards.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.530
Whether it's the past or the future

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.620
or, of course, the present,

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:20.030
I am the one that has to shoulder it.

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:24.710
You'll understand the meaning to everything afterwards.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.350
So let's worry!

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:28.960
even if you don't understand them now,

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:33.630
whether it has to do with pain, fortune or secrets.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:38.040
So don't cry, let's hold each other as we go

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:41.520
forever-

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:47.270
It's My Life dakara

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:47.270
It's My Life

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:47.280
because it's my life.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:45.970
last frame of Manabi Straight! logo

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.550
The last day of summer vacation...

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:56.120
Summer vacation's about to end!

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.870
Have you finished your homework?

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:00.510
All-nighters! All-nighters!

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:02.370
Fight-Oh!

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:06.970
Look, look!

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:09.260
The beach there was so gorgeous!

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.800
Ah, I knew they weren't listening.

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:17.280
The summer vacation that we thought was long...

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.150
...but alas, time flew.

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:23.350
Every time we gathered, we ended up in play mode.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:25.320
Looking back,

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:27.530
at the closing ceremony of the first semester...

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.180
Well then, in one month,

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:32.740
Note: Japanese schools' summer vacation go from end of July to end of August.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.740
see you again on September 1st.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.000
By then...

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.590
They seem to have high expectations.

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:47.520
But just one month?

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:48.960
More than enough time.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.800
...or so we thought.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.870
Who was it that said we had more than enough time?!

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:57.180
You, yourself.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.430
Wake up!

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:13.700
You'll die if you sleep!

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:15.770
We've stayed here for two days in a row already.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.340
It's too much to ask, I guess.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.490
Hey, hey, do I smell funny?

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.200
Why does octopus's kanji have a bug as its radical?

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.560
They're not bugs...

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:26.560
Why is herring's kanji read as "not fish"?

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:29.000
Is everyone making fun of herrings?

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.970
Manabi-chan?

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.220
I've got a great idea!

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:34.840
Let's rearrange the room!

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.090
A great leap forward!

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:39.720
...what?

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.530
Once we rearrange the look of the room,

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:43.620
everything will start working out just fine.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:45.550
I think that's the only thing we can do!

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.820
Room rearrangement!

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.480
If we move the tables around,
we'll make a great leap forward!

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:51.910
See? Isn't this place great for the sun?

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:53.110
Really, really good, right?

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:56.120
Even feng-shui-wise, the alpha waves get pissed, too!

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:58.820
Then, things will start working out!

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:00.690
I think that's the only thing we can do!

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:03.120
Right? The little people think so, too, right?

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.910
Right? Right?

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:05.660
Right?

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:06.670
Calm down, Manabi-

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:07.500
Go!

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:08.820
Forward, go!

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:09.700
Manabi! Ouch!

00:05:08.820 --> 00:06:02.700
Forward, go!

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:10.420
Wait- Ouch!

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:13.080
Manabi-chan's broken down!

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.760
What should we do?

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:15.730
Leave it to me.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:16.760
Mei-chan!

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:19.790
Wake up!

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:20.900
You'll die if you sleep!

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:24.580
You're the one that needs to wake up!

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:26.280
Mikan, do something!

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:28.810
Men shouldn't be blaming problems on others!

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:30.340
I'm a girl to begin with!

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:32.450
"D-Do something", but...

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:34.360
Momo-chan!

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:38.000
Want some?

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:40.900
Oh, ignoring me?

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:41.620
Ignoring me again?

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:51.020
You're a man; aren't you
ashamed to be wearing a skirt?!

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:53.960
Stop it!

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:54.920
Don't strip me!

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:31.050
You dumb girl!

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:33.460
You think we can keep on winning by doing something like that?

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:35.370
Forgive me, senpai.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:37.200
I did the wrong thing.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:40.380
No, you taught me a good lesson.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:41.720
Senpai!

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:47.040
Hey, can I say something?

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:51.950
We're forgetting about something important, aren't we?

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:52.880
What's that?

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:53.960
Can I say it?

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:54.830
Go ahead.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.280
Can I really say it?

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.440
I said, go ahead.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:06:58.740
Then, here I go.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.140
We've forgot to do summer homew-

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.240
Wahhh!!

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:05.820
We've forgot to do summer homew-

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:06.280
Wah!!

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:08.250
And you're out!

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:12.730
Umm, at this rate...

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:14.890
...we're all going to die...

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:16.700
So, I propose that...

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:18.810
...we take turns...

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:20.260
...catching some sleep...

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.240
Whoever wants to go first,

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:25.940
come write down your name where you like.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:31.940
It's too much trouble to even stand up, right?

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:32.770
Yeah.

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:41.820
Ah, look, look!

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:44.030
This restaurant was really delicious-

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:47.530
They're gone...

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:53.330
It's so warm and comfortable.

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:55.500
Yeah...

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:58.070
I wish we could've gone to the beach.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:00.050
Yeah...

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:04.340
Summer vacation ends today, right?

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:05.760
Yeah...

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:10.740
It was fun, right?

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:12.560
Yeah...

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.480
When I woke up,

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:36.150
I was standing in the middle of some street.

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:57.240
Where was everyone?

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:01.320
No matter how hard I looked,

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:05.380
I couldn't find them anywhere.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.360
Mikan-chan!

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.430
Hey!

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.680
Over here, over here!

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:23.550
Hurry up!

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:35.150
Look at her; she's so happy.

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:37.160
I wonder what kind of dream she's having.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:40.710
Let's leave her like this for a bit longer.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:41.960
Yeah.

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:57.120
Oh, isn't this shirt the one you've been wanting?

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:57.830
You bought it?

00:09:58.400 --> 00:09:59.960
Yeah, with my pay.

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:01.420
Lucky...

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:04.210
Maybe I should quit being a student, too.

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:06.880
Hey, being part of the work force is pretty fun.

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:08.810
Every day's like a festival.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.930
Next stop is Seioh Lower Hill.

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:15.460
Seioh Lower Hill.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:35.940
No, I should get this one.

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.580
No, actually...

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:41.380
Dragon...

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:43.380
Welcome!

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:10.510
I'm sorry, really...

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:11.780
Don't worry about it.

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:16.260
Manabi-chan really likes oojikintoki, so she'll be really happy.

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:16.260
Note: Oojikintoki is a type of red bean snack.

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:17.140
Really?

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:18.200
That's great.

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:22.330
U-Umm...

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:23.540
Yes?

00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:26.550
Takako-san, you're so beautiful!

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:28.740
Thank you.

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:38.820
Awesome...

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:43.300
Oojikin... the best!

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:44.360
Itadakimasu.

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:52.300
Interesting.

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:53.820
Interesting, indeed.

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:56.130
Thanks for the snacks, Takako-san.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:57.240
Don't mention it.

00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:02.750
Note: The website is a log of what happened during
the first half of summer break: no sleep, working non-stop, etc.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:59.940
Operation Daily Log

00:11:57.490 --> 00:12:00.880
Because when I saw Seioh Web's operation daily log...

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:06.380
I read that you guys have been staying here every night.

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:07.750
My, my!

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:11.530
To thank you, let me show you some photos of Hawaii!

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:13.510
The beach and restaurant here-

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:18.540
So, is the Aikoh President here to scout on us?

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:16.020
Ah, I'm talking to myself, huh?

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:18.360
Hey, am I talking to myself?

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:19.970
Mei-chan!

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:22.270
You're the webmaster for Seioh Web, right?

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:25.270
I think you did a great job.

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:30.540
Oh, I heard her heart skip a beat.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:32.030
Yeah, I heard it, too.

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:33.950
And another thing,

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:37.420
I wanted to discuss something with Manabi-san.

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:43.960
Over here, over here!

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:45.120
Over here,

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:48.420
we'll make a HUGE gate!

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:51.570
When we make a large order of materials from Home Center,

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:53.720
we get a bit of a discount deal!

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:58.060
Over there we plan on having booths and booths of food.

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:01.720
And on that quad there,
we'll have a flea market going on, too!

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:05.130
And over there will be a stall by Haneda-san of class 2-C.

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:08.120
And over there will be a stall by Miwa-san of class 1-B.

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:11.770
And over there will be something by Yamamoto-san and his friends from class 2-D.

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:14.050
Over there is Araki-san's group,

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:18.550
and on the field will be Kudou-san and Watanabe-san and Sawamura-san's-

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:19.280
Wait!

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:24.540
Do you remember all this?

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:28.790
The arrangement of whose store is where and what they're doing.

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:33.510
I can see it.

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:35.110
You can see it?

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:36.800
Yeah.

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:15.370
Come on!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:25.550
Go, go, go, go!

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:31.500
Thank you.

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:34.960
Huh?

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:39.210
Taka-chan, you lit the fire in us.

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:42.210
Every day's so much fun now...

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:43.530
...thanks to you, Taka-chan.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:45.640
Thank you!

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:48.520
I'll take you around this part, too!

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:49.030
Come!

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:55.270
Merger?

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:58.770
SUPERINTENDENT

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:57.460
We're taking them in,

00:15:57.460 --> 00:15:58.570
to be precise.

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:01.370
The decrease in the number of students,

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:02.960
the deadlock in their administration...

00:16:03.550 --> 00:16:04.760
In this day and age,

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:07.530
it's really not surprising to see them run a school aimlessly like they are.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:11.430
As for things like preserving or changing the Seioh name,

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:13.550
we haven't decided on those small details.

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:15.470
But sooner or later,

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:19.930
Seioh High School will be merged and acquired by us, Aikoh High School.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:23.460
You...

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:27.230
...have a personal relationship with
Seioh's Student Council President, right?

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:30.010
What does that have...

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:31.820
To be honest,

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:34.350
I was thinking about canceling their School Fair.

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:39.710
Their School Fair is straightforward evidence that Seioh is being run in the wrong way.

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:44.240
Such temporal, harebrained, meaningless festivals.

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:45.640
But this is all too sudden!

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:46.860
At least, wait until next year-

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:48.660
They are still in the planning phase.

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:50.690
We think there's nothing harmful in doing so.

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:52.300
But...

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.060
Then let me say this.

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:59.000
Unlike the many youngsters today that search for more fun by leaving school,

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:03.270
you, who have chosen to stay as students, are right now...

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:06.650
...organizing a festival just to have fun;
what's the meaning to that?

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:13.140
We are planning to make this announcement public on September 1st.

00:17:13.730 --> 00:17:18.420
Prepare a public statement as our Student Council President to be read on that day.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:22.280
Of course, keep this information to yourself.

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:24.040
Do I make myself clear?

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:31.330
Yes, ma'am.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:55.730
Uehara-san, there are glaring errors in the data you inputted.

00:17:55.730 --> 00:17:56.860
Please be more careful.

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:57.660
My bad.

00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:58.690
I'll be more careful.

00:17:58.690 --> 00:17:59.620
Don't mind.

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:00.460
Fight-o!

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:01.370
One shot.

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:04.780
Senpai.

00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:07.450
Senpai, I've always...

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:09.510
Sorry, I-

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:11.990
Senpai, you liar!

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:12.820
Wait!

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:15.510
Lie? What lie? Huh?

00:18:18.060 --> 00:18:19.620
Sorry, Taka-chan.

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:22.080
Letting you just sit there.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:24.630
Oh, no, don't worry about it.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:29.290
Hey.

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:34.310
Why are you all working so hard for this?

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:37.310
Hmm, let's see...

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:40.140
Because it's fun?

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:42.050
And it makes us happy?

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:45.930
We as a group are preparing something, right?

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.190
And then when everyone sees it,

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:50.160
they're all very happy,

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:51.520
which also makes us happy.

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:52.420
Yeah!

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:53.640
Indeed.

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:55.200
Not for me, though.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:56.730
There you go, again.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:58.580
Mei-tan, you're such a tsundere.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:58.580
Note: Tsundere refers to a person who is insincere with their true feelings.

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:00.290
Huh?

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:01.910
Ignoring me 'till the end, eh?

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:05.340
Are you going back?

00:19:05.550 --> 00:19:07.840
If you could wait a bit more, we can go together-

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:11.160
No, there's something I need to do.

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:14.570
Quit complaining already.

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:16.050
Bye bye, Taka-chan.

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:50.210
I couldn't see it...

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:52.760
...see Manabi's image...

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:58.230
The "something" that only we students can accomplish in that place...

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:01.350
Perhaps, the answer to that is...

